		(uuid "089f0626-adc3-4f83-960b-f289f3b7d1ce")
	)
	(text "GND: single board ground. J7 pin 2 (5 V\nreturn) is GND. The DDR-60L-5 isolates it\nfrom the 48 V battery. No motor current\nflows on this board, so there is no\nseparate power ground. The CAN bus side has its\nown isolated ground (GND_ISO, CAN sheet), fed\nfrom a separate isolated 24 V converter.\nGND_ISO never joins GND or CHASSIS."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 33.02 150 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "120190f1-7e51-4ae3-bd17-292a4bb8a6f3")
	)
	(text "STM32G474 CANopen master\n+ isolated CAN"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 130.34 46.85 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3c8adaf1-b8c7-4e86-a60b-67ae3b5d14c4")
	)
	(text "H1/H2/H3/H4: M3 plated mounting holes\non CHASSIS. Bond to the metal enclosure\nor dish frame.\nH5: M2.5 hole, no copper, for the standoff\nof a J3 HAT board (M2.5 x 11 mm)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 114.3 168.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3dbbbecf-78b9-4304-a3c7-63acf4c8de87")
	)
	(text "Raspberry Pi CM5 + STM32 CANopen\nServo Dish Controller"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.272 17 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 5 5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6cf1a1eb-0278-4bed-8ea7-c093b259d92d")
	)
	(text "Pi CM5 Module + IO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 198.92 76.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "76d87bea-069f-4001-817c-9adf6256149a")
	)
	(text "C70: second HF bond (2 kV, as\nC1), at the USB connectors. The\nboard is open inside the metal\nbox, so the USB shells have no\npanel bond."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 127 186.69 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8773e0a7-2a26-4c08-82de-204e1c0c01a3")
	)
	(text "R1/C1: CHASSIS-GND static bleed (R1) and HF\nbond (C1, keep 2 kV). Connector shields (RJ45,\nUSB, CAN) and the Ethernet termination (P10)\ngo to CHASSIS. Installed, GND is also bonded\nto the box at the J8 antenna arrestor, so R1\nis bypassed at DC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 186.69 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a71bddb7-cf07-4ee3-a983-2b6d5d94dbea")
	)
	(text "48 V battery -> Mean Well DDR-60L-5 (external,\nisolated DIN-rail converter) -> 5 V -> J7\n48 V -> isolated 48 V to 24 V converter (external)\n-> 24 V -> J13 on the CAN sheet (isolated bus side)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 60.96 73.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a8d24958-4166-481e-9908-4953ffbf416f")
	)
	(text "Derived from the roboclaw-cm4-dc-dish-controller board. Changes:\n- RoboClaw and all motor, encoder and limit-switch circuitry removed. No motor power on this board.\n- STM32G474RET6 in its place: CANopen master for the servo drives (e.g. DSY-400C) on one isolated CAN bus.\n  It closes the position / velocity loop over CAN and talks to the CM5 over a UART.\n- 5 V DC input from an external Mean Well DDR-60L-5 isolated converter on the 48 V battery (was 12 V battery and an on-board buck).\n- CM5 replaces the CM4. Its two USB 3.0 ports go to a stacked USB 3.0 Type-A connector (the USB 2.0 hub is gone).\nSchematic only so far: no PCB layout."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 171 150 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b6c685df-3c76-42f5-b2a2-b632b52a7131")
	)
	(text "GPS 1PPS and NMEA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 130.34 96.38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "bc584126-b584-4426-9bc8-7192cbb9985b")
	)
	(text "5 V input, fuse, reverse\npolarity, on/off switch"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 61.76 50.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "eb10aa21-cd4c-4a20-a3cf-eb4929cefa7a")
	)
